  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR is slice S3b of #2629: the playback worker side. It stacks on nothing; S3a (#3878) is on main.\n\nThe playback gets an opt-in **layer mode** (`PlayWorker::spawn_layered(seed, cutter)`):\n\n- Before the first cut, each op gets one owner. A plain op goes to the layer when its tool is a ball or a flat end mill and its moves are linear and upright. A plain op has no rotary, turning, undercut or drill. The f64 field cuts every other op, and never a layer op.\n- `camcraft_sim::stock_sim::LayerPlay` keeps the layer: a dense f32 cut layer on the lattice of the packed frame. Its value at move k is the max-law fold of the layer moves before k. It has its own keyframes (every stride, 256 MiB budget), and it cuts only when a frame is published.\n- A cutter from the caller (`LayerCutter`) cuts each batch onto the layer. `cpu_layer_cutter` is the CPU twin law (`run_twin_items_onto`, bit-exact to the one-batch twin). In S3c the UI gives a GPU cutter on its render device.\n- A frame is `max(pack_cut(field), layer)` and is always a whole layer (`stock_play_worker_frame.rs`).\n- A layer fault (a cutter error, or a window over the twin ceiling) turns the mode off. The reason is logged. The field is then rebuilt from the uncut stock with every op, at the same position.\n\nNo caller turns the mode on in this PR, so the product picture does not change. `camcraft-app` gets no `camcraft-gpu` dependency. The worker never makes a second `wgpu` instance (#3589), and it does not use the software shared device (review of PR #3532).\n\nReview notes of PR #3878 that belong to S3b:\n- **The spot-check tie** (`crates/gpu/src/cut_run.rs` `want_at`): the bound now takes the largest claim margin of each item whose CPU value is within its own margin of the result. Before, a base value that won gave a bound of about one ULP. A spring pass over a keyframe could then refuse a good GPU layer and turn the GPU path off for the process.\n- **The device-loss `Err` of `cut_into`** is now asserted in `a_lost_device_takes_the_cpu_law_and_never_crashes`.\n\nMoves for the 400-line law: `FieldPlay::cut` moves without a change (off mode) to `crates/app/src/stock_play_cut.rs` (`stock_play.rs` 430 -> 409 lines). The frame packing moves to `crates/app/src/stock_play_worker_frame.rs` (`stock_play_worker.rs` 406 -> 359 lines).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/stock_play_picture.rs`:\n  - `the_layer_playback_draws_the_field_picture_within_the_twin_margin`: the layered worker and the field worker play the same positions, with a half-drawn move, the end, and a backward seek. At each landed frame, the drawn layer `max(mesh, cut)` of the layer worker is within the twin margin of the field worker. It never draws more removal than the field (1e-6). Each layer frame is whole.\n  - `a_layer_fault_falls_back_to_the_field_picture_bit_for_bit`: a cutter that faults at once, or after two batches (a lost GPU device). The mode goes off, and the rebuilt field is bit-equal to the field playback at the same position.\n  - `the_layer_mode_is_set_once_before_the_first_cut`.\n- `crates/sim/tests/stock_cut_twin.rs`:\n  - `the_layer_playback_is_the_one_batch_twin_at_every_seek`: forward, jump, backward and end seeks, bit-equal to the one-batch twin.\n  - `the_layer_frame_shows_the_travelled_part_of_the_move_in_flight`.\n  - `an_op_without_a_twin_stays_on_the_field_by_name`, `a_bad_base_layer_is_refused_by_name`.\n  - The existing `the_gpu_kernel_fixtures_match_the_twin` stays green after the `run_twin` refactor.\n- `crates/gpu/tests/cut_onto.rs`: `a_tie_with_the_keyframe_does_not_refuse_a_good_gpu_layer` (new), and the `cut_into` lost-device assert.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6) on 5522dfe96: green, 94 steps, 0 failed. The steps were the app, gpu and sim lib tests, every `app:stock_play*` suite, and the app and sim suites that the `sim::stock_sim` gate map reaches.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gpu -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo check -p camcraft-ui`: clean (the UI keeps `PlayWorker::spawn`).\n- Heavy lanes: none (a P2 PR gets no heavy step).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A GPU cutter: no `LayerCutter` calls `camcraft-gpu` in this slice (S3c).\n- The UI: nothing calls `spawn_layered`. In the layer mode `FieldView::stock` does not hold the layer ops' cut. So the CPU eye (`cpu_eye.rs` `march_job`) must not get a layered worker. S3c turns the mode on only with the trace eye.\n- A hardware adapter.\n\n## What remains of #2629 (S3c)\n\n- The GPU cutter: map `TwinItem` to `camcraft_gpu::CutItem`, then call `cut_onto_or_cpu_on` (or `cut_into`) on the render device, off the UI thread.\n- The UI turns the layer mode on only with the trace eye.\n- Patch frames for the layer.\n- The path choice from hardware timings.\n- The parity proof on a hardware adapter.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2629-gpu-playback-layer.md`.\n\nEffort: max.\n\nChangelog: none (an opt-in mode that no caller turns on yet)\n\nRefs #2629\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
